{"type":"message","id":"196722b5","parentId":"b3469113","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:33:13.318Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All POST requests are failing with error code 1101. This error code might be specific to the Worker's error handling. Let me check the GET endpoint again to see if it has some rate limiting.\n\nActually, looking at the GET responses, they returned data fine. The issue is specifically with POST. Error 1101 might be \"Rate limit exceeded\" or something similar in Cloudflare Workers context.\n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe I need to wait a bit longer between requests, or there's a specific format needed. Let me check if there's any documentation available.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the error - error code 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker exceeded memory limit\" or \"Worker CPU time limit\". \n\nIf that's what's happening, the Worker itself could be crashing. Though maybe 1101 is just a custom error they're using. I should test with a completely minimal payload to isolate whether it's a size or format issue.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-ae0bec7f-7c68-4992-901f-da551a171493","name":"web_fetch","arguments":{"url":"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/"},"partialArgs":"{\"url\":\"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":207,"output":230,"cacheRead":20496,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20933,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779366786065,"responseId":"chatcmpl-460f2f44-ee39-4881-8f76-be64537e7538"}}
